# User-private benchmark fixtures.
# The hand-labelled task JSONs in benchmarks/cross_repo/ encode
# repo-specific directory structure and feature vocabulary in their
# `expected` paths and `question` strings, which together identify
# the underlying codebases to anyone familiar with them. They are
# kept locally for reproduction but never tracked in version control.
# The schema (cross_repo/README.md) and the harness scripts
# (benchmarks/parity_vs_ripgrep.py, etc.) remain checked in so an
# independent reader can build their own fixtures and reproduce the
# protocol.
benchmarks/cross_repo/*.json

# User-private development directives.
# These files capture how the maintainer prefers to collaborate
# with AI assistants (Claude Code etc.) on this project — they
# encode personal methodology, project-specific instructions, and
# session-shaped preferences that aren't general guidance for
# external contributors. They're kept locally so the assistant
# picks them up via @-references but are never tracked in version
# control.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.claude.md
.claude/
.agents/
.codex/
.omc/
.superconductor/
*.local.md
*.private.md

# Local-only symlinks pointing at other private repos on the
# maintainer's machine. These were tracked at one point and showed
# up on the GitHub Pages tree as broken external links — removed
# from tracking and ignored going forward.
/<repo-A>
/<repo-B>
/<repo-C>
/<repo-D>
